## Nested `if()` Statements {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

`if` inside an `if`


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
if(condition1) {
  if(condition2) {
    statement1 
  } else {
    statement2
  }
}
```
:::


## Decide which inputs to accept {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

For numeric ages, skip missing and nonpositive values. For a factor, drop the invalid code `-1`. Stop if there are no valid ages or if the input type is unsupported.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
my_descriptives <- function(x) {
  if (is.numeric(x)) {
    ages <- x[!is.na(x) & x > 0]
    if (length(ages) == 0) stop("No valid ages left")
    summary(ages)
  } else if (is.factor(x)) {
    table(droplevels(x[x != -1]))
  } else {
    stop("Expected numeric ages or a factor")
  }
}
```
:::


