```


:::
:::


## if-else on a vector: The `ifelse()` Function {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
height <- c(69, 71, 67, 66, 72, 71, 61, 65, 73, 70, 68, 74)

if (height > 69){
  print("tall") 
} else {
  print("short")
}
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-error}

```
Error in `if (height > 69) ...`:
! the condition has length > 1
```


:::
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
htCategory <- ifelse(height > 69, yes = "tall", no = "short")

htCategory
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
 [1] "short" "tall"  "short" "short" "tall"  "tall"  "short" "short" "tall" 
[10] "tall"  "short" "tall" 
```


:::
:::


For more complicated cases we can use `apply()`

## Terminating a function with returns, errors, and warnings {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

The following functions are useful for terminating a function call or just printing a warning message:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
return()     # Terminate a function call and return a value
stop()       # Terminate a function call and print an error message
warning()    # Print a warning message (without terminating the function call)
```
:::


## Terminating a Function Call Using `return()` {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
mySign <- function(x) {
  if(x < 0) return("Negative")
  if(x > 0) return("Positive")
  return("Zero")
}

mySign(x = 13)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] "Positive"
```


:::
:::


Note: `return("Zero")` not reached

## Terminating Using `stop()` {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

An `if` condition needs one `TRUE` or `FALSE`. Check that `y` is one nonmissing number before comparing it to zero.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio <- function(x, y) {
  if (!is.numeric(y) || length(y) != 1 || is.na(y)) {
    stop("y must be one nonmissing number")
  }
  if (y == 0) stop("Cannot divide by 0")
  x / y
}
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio(3, 2) # Valid input
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 1.5
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio(3, 0) # Zero denominator
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-error}

```
Error in `myRatio()`:
! Cannot divide by 0
```


:::
:::


## Test the denominator check {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

Each of these inputs fails the check before R compares `y` to zero.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio(3, c(1, 2))   # More than one value
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-error}

```
Error in `myRatio()`:
! y must be one nonmissing number
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio(3, numeric()) # No values
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-error}

```
Error in `myRatio()`:
! y must be one nonmissing number
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio(3, NA_real_)  # Missing value
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-error}

```
Error in `myRatio()`:
! y must be one nonmissing number
```


:::
:::


## Printing a Warning Message Using `warning()` {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

`warning()` reports a problem and lets the function continue.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
myRatio <- function(x, y) {
  if (!is.numeric(y) || length(y) != 1 || is.na(y)) {
    stop("y must be one nonmissing number")
  }
  if (y == 0) warning("Attempt made to divide by 0")
  x / y
}

myRatio(x = 3, y = 0)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}

```
Warning in myRatio(x = 3, y = 0): Attempt made to divide by 0
```


:::

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] Inf
```


:::
:::


In this example, `3 / 0` returns `Inf` after the warning.

## Looping {data-background-image="./_extensions/emc/www/triangle1.svg" data-background-size="contain" data-background-position="top left"}

Repeat (iterate) an R statement


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
for() # Repeat a set of statements a specified number of times
while() # Repeat a set of statements as long as a specified condition is met
repeat # Repeat a set of statements until a break command is encountered
```
:::


Stopping a loop:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
break # Terminate a loops iterations
next # Skip ahead to the next iteration
```
:::


